B.bf4=s(["about","overview","start","what is this","purpose","tabs","navigation","where"],t.s)
B.aoC=new A.jl("what-is-no-sus","What NO SUS is","Home is everything you keep. The Send button is everything you give away.",B.Kw,B.biy,B.bf4)
B.apU=new A.aQ(63023,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.ao4=new A.d2("Where it lives","In a NO SUS folder in your own Google Drive. NO SUS can open only the files it creates there, so connecting does not let it see the rest of your Drive.",!1)
B.anY=new A.d2("Adding to it","Open Chat, then You. Type a note or attach a file. You can also share something to NO SUS from another app: it opens Send with You already picked.",!1)
B.aoj=new A.d2("Before Drive is connected","What you add waits on this phone as Not saved yet, and is stored as soon as you connect.",!1)
B.b0H=s([B.ao4,B.anY,B.aoj],t.eH)
B.bi_=s(["saved","you","drive","google drive","notes to self","library","keep"],t.s)
B.aoA=new A.jl("no-sus-chat","NO SUS Chat","A chat with yourself for notes, links and files, kept in your own Google Drive.",B.apU,B.b0H,B.bi_)
B.anV=new A.d2("How","On the other screen, open nosus.foo/go. On your phone, open Chat, tap Open on any screen and scan the QR it shows. Match the number, then choose what that screen can open.",!1)
B.aon=new A.d2("Your account stays on your phone","The other screen only gets the items you approve, and only while the session is open.",!1)
B.ao8=new A.d2("After the session","Ending the session stops that screen from opening anything else. Files you downloaded or printed there can stay on it, so use a screen you trust.",!0)
B.bej=s([B.anV,B.aon,B.ao8],t.eH)
B.bhh=s(["go","computer","borrowed","laptop","qr","scan","print","desk"],t.s)
B.aoJ=new A.jl("open-on-any-screen","Open on any screen","Open your own chat on a computer without signing in to Google there.",B.lV,B.bej,B.bhh)
B.ao6=new A.d2("What and where","Choose a file or write a note. Send it to You, to one of your groups, or to Anyone with a link. Anyone with a link needs no account to open it.",!1)
B.ao_=new A.d2("How it opens","For a link, turn on one of: One open, Watermarked, or Traceable copies. Each one says what it does right under it.",!1)
B.anL=new A.d2("Opening a link or code","Send \u2192 Open a link or code. Codes work once and expire.",!1)
B.aos=new A.d2("Sending nearby","Sending between two phones on the same Wi-Fi was removed. Send a link instead.",!1)
B.bbN=s([B.ao6,B.ao_,B.anL,B.aos],t.eH)
B.bg5=s(["share","send","link","share sheet","nearby","receive","address","drop"],t.s)
B.aoE=new A.jl("send","Send","One flow: what, where, how.",B.KD,B.bbN,B.bg5)
B.aor=new A.d2("How it works","It is encrypted on your phone first. The key goes in the link, after the # sign, which browsers never send to a server. The first person to open the link gets it, and the stored copy is deleted.",!1)
B.anH=new A.d2("Limits","Up to 10 files and 50 MB together in one link. Instead of a link you can ask for a 6-digit code to type in. While that code is unused, a copy of the key is kept on our server for up to 10 minutes.",!1)
B.aoe=new A.d2("It really is one open","If a chat app previews the link, that counts as the open. The person then sees that it was already opened, which tells you something got to it first.",!0)
B.anT=new A.d2("Did they open it?","Links you sent, on Send, shows if each one was opened and when. Nobody learns who opened it. Signed in, you are told when it happens: to do that, our server knows which account sent which link (never what is in it) until it is opened or expires. Turn off Link opened in Settings \u2192 Notifications and new links are not tied to you. Not signed in, a link is tied to no one.",!1)
B.bf2=s([B.aor,B.anH,B.aoe,B.anT],t.eH)
